omponents":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The biconnected components (blocks) of an undirected graph: a collection of blocks, each the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"positions of its edges in ascending order; blocks are ordered by their smallest edge position.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The blocks partition the edges that are not self-loops.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/biconnectedcomponents","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/BiconnectedComponents","title":"BiconnectedComponents","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BiconnectedComponents"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BiconnectedComponents"}]},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/BlockCutTree":{"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/blockcuttree","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BlockCutTree","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BlockCutTree","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The block–cut tree of an undirected graph (Harary’s block-cutpoint tree): a node per block and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per articulation point, and an edge joining each block to each articulation point it contains."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Blocks are numbered as in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"blocks"},{"type":"text","text":", articulation points by their place in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"articulationPoints"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order). It is a forest: one tree per connected component with an edge that is not a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"self-loop; isolated vertices are no node.","type":"text"}],"title":"BlockCutTree","kind":"symbo